Yay, finally made it! Used to play for years back in the 90's without
making it. Got close a few times, but no cigar. Resumed playing in the
last few months, and it's such a great game! Still the best out there.

Long story short: Healer/Gnome/Female, playing semi-pacifist for AC
boost in minetown. Ascended at XP level 19, stayed at AC -35 for the
second half of the game, HP peaked at 200, but Death knocked it down
to 123 in the Astral plane. Not close to dying, never had use for
AoLS. Game took about 8 days, with between 1 and 3 hours playing each
day. What did it for me was patience. I never took big risks, read all
the messages carefully, explored the entire dungeon from bottom to top
several times. Maniac's guide was extremely helpful. Biggest obstacle
was getting a ring of levitation for the air plane, but I managed to
find one on a randomly generated monster when I was doing the
Ascension run! I found lots of wands of death, so Rodney and friends
never posed any serious problems.

